      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> The task requires creating a Python file named extract_json.py that calls a hosted LLM to extract structured JSON from text. The implementation must use a concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in the code. I will choose Amazon Bedrock as the external provider because it is a well-known service for accessing various foundation models, including those capable of extracting structured data. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789854684783,
          "start": 1789854681864
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bba70b08001qFj50Kv2XO3nM6",
